desc:VAL60 [valve compressor] (GFX Lab)
//tags: channel strip valve tube transistor transformer preamp compressor saturation warmth
//author: JGWizrad / Garden FX (GFX)
//
// Requires gfx-lab-drift, gfx-lab-output, gfx-lab-thick, gfx-lab-glow, gfx-lab-os, gfx-lab-bypass (.jsfx-inc) in
// the same folder.
//
// VAL60 (Lab) - a channel with a stackable preamp: in the spirit of the 1990s British dual-channel valve dynamics
// processors that put a tube gain stage in front of a soft-knee, optical-style compressor. The original had one
// valve stage; this one has four - IRON, TRANSISTOR, SOLID STATE and VALVE - each switched in by a click on its
// name, with its own DRIVE, run in any order: each module's < > keys move it along the stack (the panel shows the order).
//
// SIGNAL FLOW
//   input transformer > INPUT GAIN > GUARD (off by default: the house input guard - eases hot sources down towards
//   -18 dBFS and catches peaks above -6 dBFS, never boosts) > the PREAMP STACK (the four stages left to right as on the panel, oversampled
//   1x / 2x / 4x: the OS key)
//   > THICK > soft-knee compressor (THRESHOLD, RATIO, ATTACK, RELEASE; an optical-style memory: after heavy, long
//   compression the release slows, up to 2x) > MAKE-UP, MIX > output transformer > LEVEL > the house output stage
//   (CLIP, -0.3 dBFS) > BYPASS.
//   The stages (each keeps its level, so DRIVE adds harmonics, not volume; each has its own gentle voicing, there
//   whenever it is in - JG: iron pushed lows, transistor a mid lift, solid state pushed highs, valve a mid dip):
//     IRON         a transformer core: only the lows saturate (below about 150 Hz), mostly 3rd harmonic, the top
//                  stays clean - weight and a firmer bottom; voicing +2.5 dB low shelf at 120 Hz
//     TRANSISTOR   a single-ended discrete stage: lop-sided (2nd harmonic), and the highs drive it harder than the
//                  lows (pre-emphasis in, de-emphasis out) - a forward, crisp edge; voicing +2 dB at 1.5 kHz
//     SOLID STATE  an op-amp stage: clean until it nears the rails, then a firm, symmetrical knee (odd harmonics);
//                  voicing +2.5 dB high shelf at 7 kHz
//     VALVE        the original VAL60 valve: a biased triode, soft and asymmetric; voicing -2 dB at 700 Hz
//   A click on a stage's name (lit in its colour = in) crossfades it in or out (12 ms); PREAMP: the whole stack in or out. Moving a stage
//   (< >) crossfades (5 ms) out of the stack, reorders, and comes back.
//   Init = order IRON, TRANSISTOR, SOLID STATE, VALVE with only VALVE in, OS 2x: the Stable VAL60's sound plus the
//   valve's mid dip.
//   IN: the compressor in or out; MAKE-UP (0 - 20 dB) on the compressed path; MIX: parallel compression.
//   BYPASS (the house key): crossfades (15 ms) to the untouched input, delayed by the latency.
// THRESHOLD is in dBu (0 dBu = -18 dBFS, the house calibration), -20 .. +20 dBu, default 0 dBu (JG, 29 Oct 2026: the
// Stable range -30 .. +10, default -10, was too sensitive - 7 dB of gain reduction on a 0 VU programme at the default).
//
// THICK: the house THICK circuit (gfx-lab-thick), between the preamp and the compressor; every stage is also pushed
//   harder (the valves more lop-sided), the input transformer loaded more and the detector window lengthened to 25 ms.
// DRIFT (a key: 33 % lit, 5 % dark; 50 % = the standard amount below): each stage in the stack drifts its own way
//   (only the stages in use):
//     valve        warm-up from load (a little quieter and more lop-sided, settling over about a minute: the
//                  HEATERS lamp), heater wander of bias (+/- 0.04) and gain (+/- 0.15 dB), HT sag on loud programme
//                  (up to 15 % more drive, the level dips to -0.25 dB)
//     iron         the core's temperature: its saturation point wanders (+/- 8 %)
//     transistor   bias wanders (+/- 0.05) and creeps up as the stage heats on loud programme (+0.08 over seconds)
//     solid state  the rails sag on peaks: it clips a little earlier (up to 12 %)
//     compressor   the timing parts sit off nominal (+/- 8 %) and wander (+/- 6 %)
//   0 % = none (and no warm-up), 100 % = twice the standard amount, a little faster.
//
// GUI: house dark grey rack faceplate, elephant's breath outlines and title; the PREAMP STACK across the top (one
//   module per stage: its name (click = in / out), DRIVE and < > keys), COMPRESSOR and OUTPUT below; BYPASS, OS and S / M / L / ? in the
//   header; drag knobs (Shift = fine), mouse wheel, double-click or Ctrl-click = default.
// PRESETS (each uses the stack: its stages, their order, THICK, GUARD; level-matched to the input on programme by
//   LEVEL, except Init, which has no make-up gain, as the Stable VAL60):
//   Init (VALVE only), Valve Warmth DI (iron > valve), Rich Bass Guitar (heavy iron > valve, THICK), Vocal Tube
//   Fatten (transistor > valve, GUARD), Drum Bus Crunch (transistor > solid state, THICK), Synth Thickening (valve >
//   iron, THICK), Acoustic Warmth (valve > solid state air), Master Bus Glue (light iron > valve), Saturated Parallel
//   (all four, MIX 50 %), Subtle Colour (iron > valve, compressor out), Console Edge (solid state > transistor), Hot
//   Source Tamer (GUARD, transistor > valve).
// Latency: 0 / 31 / 37 samples at OS 1x / 2x / 4x (default 2x), reported.
//
// TWEAK points are marked TWEAK.
// STATUS: Lab (experimental, may change), Hybrid rework of the Stable VAL60. v0.2 (checkpoint 2: fixed stage modules, < > order keys).

in_pin:left input
in_pin:right input
out_pin:left output
out_pin:right output

import gfx-lab-drift.jsfx-inc
import gfx-lab-output.jsfx-inc
import gfx-lab-thick.jsfx-inc
import gfx-lab-glow.jsfx-inc
import gfx-lab-os.jsfx-inc
import gfx-lab-bypass.jsfx-inc

slider1:c_in=1<0,1,1{Out,In}>-Compressor in
slider2:in_gain=0<-10,20,0.1>-Input gain (dB)
slider3:drv_va=20<0,100,1>-Valve drive (%)
slider4:v_on=1<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Preamp stack
slider5:thr=0<-20,20,0.1>-Threshold (dBu)
slider6:ratio=3<1.5,10,0.01>-Ratio
slider7:atk=10<1,50,0.1>-Attack (ms)
slider8:rel=500<100,4000,1>-Release (ms)
slider9:out_lvl=0<-18,6,0.1>-Level (dB)
slider10:drift=33<0,100,1>-Drift (%)
slider11:vu_mode=0<0,1,1{Output,Gain reduction}>-VU meter
slider12:thick=0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Thick
slider13:mkup=0<0,20,0.1>-Make-up gain (dB)
slider14:mix=100<0,100,1>-Mix (%)
slider15:on_ir=0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Iron stage
slider16:on_tr=0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Transistor stage
slider17:on_ss=0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Solid state stage
slider18:on_va=1<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Valve stage
slider19:drv_ir=30<0,100,1>-Iron drive (%)
slider20:drv_tr=30<0,100,1>-Transistor drive (%)
slider21:drv_ss=30<0,100,1>-Solid state drive (%)
slider22:os_sel=1<0,2,1{1x,2x,4x}>-Oversampling
slider23:byp=0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Bypass
slider24:st_ord=0<0,23,1>-Stage order (0 = iron, transistor, solid state, valve)
slider25:guard=0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Guard
slider26:prs_sel=0<0,12,1{No preset,Init,Valve Warmth DI,Rich Bass Guitar,Vocal Tube Fatten,Drum Bus Crunch,Synth Thickening,Acoustic Warmth,Master Bus Glue,Saturated Parallel,Subtle Colour,Console Edge,Hot Source Tamer}>-Preset

@init
XCH = 7400000;                               // channels 3 - 64 (8192 each): delayed by the latency too
#ui_man = "gfx-lab-val60";
ext_noinit = 1;
!ui_dflt ? ( ui_sz = 0;  pr_cur = 1; );
ui_dflt = 1;
gfx_ext_retina = 1;
CR = 16;

ost_init(0);  ostL.ost_ch_init();  ostR.ost_ch_init();

// ---------- tuning (TWEAK) ----------
K_LO = 0.08;  K_HI = 3.2;     // valve drive at DRIVE 0 % and 100 % (k = K_LO x (K_HI / K_LO) ^ drive)
V_B = 0.20;                   // the valve's bias: its even harmonics
IR_LO = 0.3;  IR_HI = 8;      // iron: core drive at 0 / 100 %
IR_F = 150;                   // iron: the lows that saturate the core (Hz)
TR_LO = 0.15;  TR_HI = 5;     // transistor: drive at 0 / 100 %
TR_B = 0.35;                  // transistor: its bias (lop-sided: 2nd harmonic)
TR_F = 2500;  TR_E = 1;       // transistor: pre-emphasis above TR_F, +6 dB (1 + TR_E = x 2)
SS_LO = 0.2;  SS_HI = 6;      // solid state: drive at 0 / 100 %
// each stage's voicing (JG, 28 Oct 2026): a gentle tone curve after its curve, there whenever the stage is in
EQ_IR_F = 120;   EQ_IR_G = 2.5;            // iron: pushed lows (low shelf, Hz / dB)
EQ_TR_F = 1500;  EQ_TR_G = 2;   EQ_TR_Q = 0.8;    // transistor: a mid lift (bell)
EQ_SS_F = 7000;  EQ_SS_G = 2.5;            // solid state: pushed highs (high shelf)
EQ_VA_F = 700;   EQ_VA_G = -2;  EQ_VA_Q = 0.7;    // valve: a mid dip (bell)
EQC = 1000;                   // memory: the voicing biquads, 5 each per stage (b0 b1 b2 a1 a2 at EQC + 5 x stage)
KNEE = 10;                    // dB: soft knee
XI_K = 0.45;  XO_K = 0.35;    // the transformers' cores

os_design();
os_f = os_tf = os_f2n(os_sel);  os_base = 0;
os_gsetup();

// ---------- drift sources ----------
HB.drift_init(0.8 + rand(1) * 0.4);   HG.drift_init(0.7 + rand(1) * 0.4);
CPA.drift_init(0.5 + rand(1) * 0.4);  CPB.drift_init(0.5 + rand(1) * 0.4);
D1.drift_init(0.6 + rand(1) * 0.5);  D2.drift_init(0.6 + rand(1) * 0.5);  D3.drift_init(0.6 + rand(1) * 0.5);  D4.drift_init(0.6 + rand(1) * 0.5);
tol_a = rand(2) - 1;  tol_r = rand(2) - 1;
warm_t = 0;

function db2g(d) ( exp(d * 0.11512925464970228); );
function g2db(g) ( 8.685889638065035 * log(max(g, 0.0000000001)); );
function ts(x) ( x = max(-3, min(3, x));  x * (27 + x * x) / (27 + 9 * x * x); );
function dts(b) local(u, v) ( u = 27 + 9 * b * b;  v = 27 + b * b;  ((27 + 3 * b * b) * u - b * v * 18 * b) / (u * u); );
function xfmr(x, k) instance(lp) (
  lp += (x - lp) * xf_c;
  x - lp + ts(lp * k) / k;
);
// RBJ biquads at the oversampled rate: kind 0 low shelf, 1 bell, 2 high shelf (shelves at slope 1)
function eq_set(t, kind, f, gdb, q, fs) local(ea, w, cw, al, a0, sq, c) (
  ea = 10 ^ (gdb / 40);  w = 2 * $pi * min(f, 0.45 * fs) / fs;  cw = cos(w);  c = EQC + 5 * t;
  kind == 1 ? (
    al = sin(w) / (2 * q);  a0 = 1 + al / ea;
    c[0] = (1 + al * ea) / a0;  c[1] = -2 * cw / a0;  c[2] = (1 - al * ea) / a0;  c[3] = -2 * cw / a0;  c[4] = (1 - al / ea) / a0;
  ) : (
    al = sin(w) / 2 * sqrt(2);  sq = 2 * sqrt(ea) * al;
    kind == 0 ? (
      a0 = (ea + 1) + (ea - 1) * cw + sq;
      c[0] = ea * ((ea + 1) - (ea - 1) * cw + sq) / a0;  c[1] = 2 * ea * ((ea - 1) - (ea + 1) * cw) / a0;
      c[2] = ea * ((ea + 1) - (ea - 1) * cw - sq) / a0;  c[3] = -2 * ((ea - 1) + (ea + 1) * cw) / a0;
      c[4] = ((ea + 1) + (ea - 1) * cw - sq) / a0;
    ) : (
      a0 = (ea + 1) - (ea - 1) * cw + sq;
      c[0] = ea * ((ea + 1) + (ea - 1) * cw + sq) / a0;  c[1] = -2 * ea * ((ea - 1) + (ea + 1) * cw) / a0;
      c[2] = ea * ((ea + 1) + (ea - 1) * cw - sq) / a0;  c[3] = 2 * ((ea - 1) - (ea + 1) * cw) / a0;
      c[4] = ((ea + 1) - (ea - 1) * cw - sq) / a0;
    );
  );
);
// the preamp stages' rate-dependent coefficients (at the oversampled rate)
function stk_coefs() local(fs, g) (
  fs = srate * os_f;
  dc_r2 = 1 - 2 * $pi * 5 / fs;
  ir_c = 1 - exp(-2 * $pi * IR_F / fs);
  g = tan($pi * min(TR_F, 0.45 * fs) / fs);
  tr_g1 = g / (1 + g);  g /= 1 + TR_E;  tr_g2 = g / (1 + g);    // the same bilinear map: de-emphasis = the exact inverse
  eq_set(1, 0, EQ_IR_F, EQ_IR_G, 0.7, fs);  eq_set(2, 1, EQ_TR_F, EQ_TR_G, EQ_TR_Q, fs);
  eq_set(3, 2, EQ_SS_F, EQ_SS_G, 0.7, fs);  eq_set(4, 1, EQ_VA_F, EQ_VA_G, EQ_VA_Q, fs);
);
// one preamp slot: ty = its stage (0 empty, 1 iron, 2 transistor, 3 solid state, 4 valve), k = its drive, b = its
// bias (valve / transistor), sl = the curve's slope at the bias (unity small-signal gain)
function stage(x, ty, k, b, sl) instance(dx, dy, lp, z1, z2, e1, e2) local(y, u, h, v, c) (
  ty == 4 ? (
    y = (ts(x * k + b) - ts(b)) / (k * sl);
    dy = y - dx + dc_r2 * dy;  dx = y;  y = dy;
  ) : ty == 1 ? (
    lp += (x - lp) * ir_c;
    y = x - lp + ts(lp * k) / k;
  ) : ty == 2 ? (
    v = (x - z1) * tr_g1;  h = x - (v + z1);  z1 += 2 * v;          // pre-emphasis: x + TR_E x the highs
    u = x + TR_E * h;
    u = (ts(u * k + b) - ts(b)) / (k * sl);
    v = (u - z2) * tr_g2;  h = v + z2;  z2 += 2 * v;               // de-emphasis: lows + highs / (1 + TR_E)
    y = h + (u - h) / (1 + TR_E);
    dy = y - dx + dc_r2 * dy;  dx = y;  y = dy;
  ) : ty == 3 ? (
    u = x * k;  u *= u;
    y = x / sqrt(sqrt(1 + u * u));
  ) : y = x;
  ty > 0 ? (                                                       // the stage's voicing
    c = EQC + 5 * ty;
    u = c[0] * y + e1;  e1 = c[1] * y - c[3] * u + e2;  e2 = c[2] * y - c[4] * u;  y = u;
  );
  y;
);
function stage_clr() instance(dx, dy, lp, z1, z2, e1, e2) ( dx = dy = lp = z1 = z2 = e1 = e2 = 0; );
function sk_of(ty, d) (
  ty == 1 ? IR_LO * (IR_HI / IR_LO) ^ d : ty == 2 ? TR_LO * (TR_HI / TR_LO) ^ d :
  ty == 3 ? SS_LO * (SS_HI / SS_LO) ^ d : K_LO * (K_HI / K_LO) ^ d;
);
// the stack, both channels, one oversampled phase: dry in xl / xr, out pl / pr
// (each position's stage blended by its own IN fade, m1 - m4; a stage that is out is skipped)
function stack(xl, xr) local(yl, yr) (
  yl = xl;  yr = xr;
  m1 > 0 ? ( yl += (S1L.stage(yl, r1, k1, b1, l1) - yl) * m1;  yr += (S1R.stage(yr, r1, k1, b1, l1) - yr) * m1; );
  m2 > 0 ? ( yl += (S2L.stage(yl, r2, k2, b2, l2) - yl) * m2;  yr += (S2R.stage(yr, r2, k2, b2, l2) - yr) * m2; );
  m3 > 0 ? ( yl += (S3L.stage(yl, r3, k3, b3, l3) - yl) * m3;  yr += (S3R.stage(yr, r3, k3, b3, l3) - yr) * m3; );
  m4 > 0 ? ( yl += (S4L.stage(yl, r4, k4, b4, l4) - yl) * m4;  yr += (S4R.stage(yr, r4, k4, b4, l4) - yr) * m4; );
  pl = xl + (yl - xl) * stk_m;  pr = xr + (yr - xr) * stk_m;
);
// the stage order: 0 - 23 = the 24 orders of the four stages (0 = iron, transistor, solid state, valve), counted
// in dictionary order -> q1 .. q4 (the stage at each position: 1 iron, 2 transistor, 3 solid state, 4 valve)
function ord_nth(n) local(i, r) (
  r = 0;  i = 1;
  loop(4, (i == 1 ? ou1 : i == 2 ? ou2 : i == 3 ? ou3 : ou4) == 0 ? ( n == 0 && r == 0 ? r = i;  n -= 1; );  i += 1; );
  r == 1 ? ou1 = 1 : r == 2 ? ou2 = 1 : r == 3 ? ou3 = 1 : ou4 = 1;
  r;
);
function ord_dec(c) (
  c = max(0, min(23, c | 0));  ou1 = ou2 = ou3 = ou4 = 0;
  q1 = ord_nth(floor(c / 6));  q2 = ord_nth(floor((c % 6) / 2));  q3 = ord_nth(c % 2);  q4 = ord_nth(0);
);

function update_params() (
  drift_macro(drift);
  t_in = c_in >= 0.5;  t_v = v_on >= 0.5;
  t_ig = in_gain;
  t_dir = drv_ir / 100;  t_dtr = drv_tr / 100;  t_dss = drv_ss / 100;  t_dva = drv_va / 100;
  t_mir = on_ir >= 0.5;  t_mtr = on_tr >= 0.5;  t_mss = on_ss >= 0.5;  t_mva = on_va >= 0.5;
  t_thr = thr;  t_rat = ratio;  t_out = out_lvl;  t_mk = mkup;
  ord_dec(st_ord);
  os_tf = os_f2n(os_sel);
);

xf_c = 1 - exp(-2 * $pi * 120 / srate);
sm_c = 1 - exp(-CR / (0.03 * srate));
sw_c = 1 - exp(-1 / (0.012 * srate));
dk_c = 1 / (0.005 * srate);                  // a stage change: 5 ms out of the stack, swap, 5 ms back
rms_c = 1 - exp(-1 / (0.01 * srate));        // detector: 10 ms mean square ...
rms_c2 = 1 - exp(-1 / (0.025 * srate));      // ... THICK: 25 ms
thk_init();  thk_lift = 4;  thk_drv = 2.0;  thk_asym = 0.22;  thk_tr = 1.0;  thk_trim = 0;   // TWEAK: VAL60's THICK
xik = XI_K;  vb = V_B;
sag_c = 1 - exp(-1 / (0.5 * srate));
heat_c = 1 - exp(-1 / (4 * srate));          // the transistor heats over seconds
stk_coefs();
update_params();
r1 = q1;  r2 = q2;  r3 = q3;  r4 = q4;  dk = 1;
s_ig = t_ig;  s_thr = t_thr;  s_rat = t_rat;  s_out = t_out;
s_dir = t_dir;  s_dtr = t_dtr;  s_dss = t_dss;  s_dva = t_dva;
m_ir = t_mir;  m_tr = t_mtr;  m_ss = t_mss;  m_va = t_mva;
ig_g = db2g(s_ig);  out_g = db2g(s_out);  ig_i = og_i = 0;
s_mk = t_mk;  mk_g = db2g(s_mk);  mk_i = 0;
mix_c = 1 - exp(-1 / (0.03 * srate));  mix_s = mix / 100;
m_in = t_in;  m_v = t_v;
ms = 0;  gr = 0;  cg = 1;  cgi = 0;  mem = 0;  sag = 0;  heat = 0;
vg = 1;  ir_w1 = ir_w2 = ir_w3 = ir_w4 = 1;  tb1 = tb2 = tb3 = tb4 = 0;
cr_n = 0;
by_setup(23);
gd_ms = 0;  gd_ag = 1;  gd_env = 0;  gd_m = 0;
gd_msc = 1 - exp(-1 / (0.3 * srate));  gd_agc = 1 - exp(-1 / (1.2 * srate));
gd_catt = 1 - exp(-1 / (0.002 * srate));  gd_crel = 1 - exp(-1 / (0.1 * srate));

// (moved here from @gfx: the PRESET parameter loads presets on the audio side)
function param_touched(idx) ( slider_automate(2 ^ (idx - 1));  gui_dirty = 1; );
function param_touched_au(idx) ( slider_automate(2 ^ (idx - 1));  gui_dirty = 1; );
function pv(i, v) ( slider(i) = v; );
function p_init() (
  pv(25, 0);  pv(1, 1); pv(2, 0); pv(3, 20); pv(4, 1); pv(5, 0); pv(6, 3); pv(7, 10); pv(8, 500); pv(9, 0); pv(10, 33); pv(11, 0); pv(12, 0); pv(13, 0); pv(14, 100);
  pv(15, 0); pv(16, 0); pv(17, 0); pv(18, 1); pv(19, 30); pv(20, 30); pv(21, 30); pv(24, 0);
);
function load_preset(p) local(i) (
  p_init();
  p == 2 ? ( pv(2, 3); pv(3, 40); pv(5, -8); pv(6, 2); pv(7, 15); pv(8, 400); pv(9, -1.5); pv(13, 5.0); pv(15, 1); pv(19, 25); pv(24, 0); );   // Valve Warmth DI
  p == 3 ? ( pv(2, 4); pv(3, 45); pv(6, 4); pv(7, 20); pv(8, 300); pv(9, -0.3); pv(12, 1); pv(13, 8.0); pv(15, 1); pv(19, 55); pv(24, 0); );   // Rich Bass Guitar
  p == 4 ? ( pv(2, 2); pv(3, 35); pv(5, -12); pv(7, 8); pv(9, 0.6); pv(13, 9.0); pv(16, 1); pv(20, 25); pv(24, 10); pv(25, 1); );   // Vocal Tube Fatten
  p == 5 ? ( pv(2, 4); pv(3, 40); pv(6, 4); pv(8, 200); pv(9, -0.8); pv(12, 1); pv(13, 8.0); pv(16, 1); pv(17, 1); pv(18, 0); pv(20, 60); pv(21, 45); pv(24, 8); );   // Drum Bus Crunch
  p == 6 ? ( pv(2, 4); pv(3, 60); pv(5, -8); pv(6, 2.5); pv(7, 20); pv(8, 600); pv(9, -1.6); pv(12, 1); pv(13, 6.0); pv(15, 1); pv(19, 40); pv(24, 18); );   // Synth Thickening
  p == 7 ? ( pv(3, 30); pv(6, 2); pv(7, 15); pv(13, 6.5); pv(17, 1); pv(21, 20); pv(24, 1); );   // Acoustic Warmth
  p == 8 ? ( pv(3, 15); pv(5, -6); pv(6, 1.5); pv(7, 30); pv(8, 800); pv(9, -0.4); pv(13, 3.0); pv(15, 1); pv(19, 20); pv(24, 0); );   // Master Bus Glue
  p == 9 ? ( pv(2, 6); pv(3, 70); pv(5, -12); pv(6, 4); pv(7, 20); pv(8, 400); pv(9, -2.2); pv(12, 1); pv(13, 7.5); pv(14, 50); pv(15, 1); pv(16, 1); pv(17, 1); pv(19, 45); pv(20, 40); pv(21, 30); pv(24, 0); );   // Saturated Parallel
  p == 10 ? ( pv(1, 0); pv(3, 25); pv(9, -0.1); pv(15, 1); pv(19, 15); pv(24, 0); );   // Subtle Colour
  p == 11 ? ( pv(2, 2); pv(5, -10); pv(6, 3); pv(7, 5); pv(8, 250); pv(9, 1.8); pv(13, 5.0); pv(16, 1); pv(17, 1); pv(18, 0); pv(20, 40); pv(21, 50); pv(24, 14); );   // Console Edge
  p == 12 ? ( pv(3, 30); pv(5, -14); pv(6, 3); pv(7, 10); pv(8, 500); pv(9, 5.0); pv(13, 6.0); pv(16, 1); pv(20, 35); pv(24, 0); pv(25, 1); );   // Hot Source Tamer
  i = 1;  loop(21, param_touched_au(i);  i += 1; );  param_touched_au(24);  param_touched_au(25);
);

// PRESET parameter (JG, 28 Oct 2026: accessibility - a screen reader reaches the presets through REAPER's parameter list).
// A change of prs_sel (a screen reader, the host, automation) loads that preset (0 = No preset: nothing loaded); the preset bar asks through
// prs_dirty. Both load here, on the audio side only. prs_last is saved, so opening a project or recalling its
// state never reloads a preset over the saved settings.
function prs_chk() local(k) (
  prs_dirty > 0 ? (
    k = prs_dirty; prs_dirty = 0; load_preset(k);
    k <= 12 ? ( prs_sel = k; slider_automate(prs_sel); prs_cur_d = k; );
    prs_last = prs_sel;
  ) : prs_ok ? (
    prs_sel = max(0, min(12, prs_sel | 0));
    prs_sel != prs_last ? ( prs_last = prs_sel; prs_sel > 0 ? ( load_preset(prs_sel); prs_cur_d = prs_sel; ); );
  ) : ( prs_last = prs_sel | 0; prs_ok = 1; );
);
prs_ok = 0; prs_dirty = 0;

@slider
prs_chk();
update_params();

@block
prs_chk();
gui_dirty ? ( gui_dirty = 0;  update_params(); );
bdt = samplesblock / srate;
warm_t += bdt;
hsp = 0.035 * dm_s * bdt;
dsp = 0.03 * dm_s * bdt;
// DRIFT, each stage its own way (only the stages in the stack)
has_v = on_va >= 0.5;
wu = has_v ? exp(-warm_t / 22) * min(dm_a, 1) : 0;
vb = V_B + 0.04 * dm_a * HB.drift_tick(hsp) + 0.10 * wu;                     // valve bias: the symmetry
vg = has_v ? db2g(0.15 * dm_a * HG.drift_tick(hsp) - 1.0 * wu) : 1;
dw_ir = D1.drift_tick(dsp);  dw_tr = D2.drift_tick(dsp);
sag_amt = min(1, sag / 0.3);
age_a = 1 + dm_a * (0.05 * tol_a + 0.04 * CPA.drift_tick(0.02 * dm_s * bdt));
age_r = 1 + dm_a * (0.05 * tol_r + 0.04 * CPB.drift_tick(0.02 * dm_s * bdt));
ost_setup(0, 0.3, 120, 6000, -0.3, 1);                                       // house output stage: CLIP
pdc_delay = os_lat(os_f);                                                    // (ost_setup zeroes pdc_delay)
// display hand-offs
gr_disp = min(gr_disp, grmin);  grmin = 0;
vul_disp = vu_n > 0 ? vul_acc / vu_n : 0;  vur_disp = vu_n > 0 ? vur_acc / vu_n : 0;  vul_acc = vur_acc = 0;  vu_n = 0;
ipk_disp = max(ipk_disp, ipk);  opk_disp = max(opk_disp, opk);  ipk = opk = 0;
ost_clipped ? ( clip_disp = 1;  ost_clipped = 0; );
wu_disp = has_v ? wu : -1;
// the track's other channels (3 and up, e.g. stems on a multichannel bus) pass through untouched but delayed by
// the latency, so everything on the track stays in time
xch_n = min(num_ch, 64) - 2;
pdc_bot_ch = 0; pdc_top_ch = 2 + max(xch_n, 0);

@serialize
file_var(0, pr_cur);
file_var(0, ui_sz);
file_avail(0) != 0 ? file_var(0, prs_last) : prs_last = prs_sel | 0; prs_ok = 1;   // PRESET parameter: no reload on recall

@sample
by_in();
ipk = max(ipk, max(abs(spl0), abs(spl1)));                                   // IN meter (peak)
cr_n <= 0 ? (
  cr_n = CR;
  s_ig += (t_ig - s_ig) * sm_c;  s_thr += (t_thr - s_thr) * sm_c;
  s_rat += (t_rat - s_rat) * sm_c;  s_out += (t_out - s_out) * sm_c;
  s_dir += (t_dir - s_dir) * sm_c;  s_dtr += (t_dtr - s_dtr) * sm_c;  s_dss += (t_dss - s_dss) * sm_c;  s_dva += (t_dva - s_dva) * sm_c;
  ig_i = (db2g(s_ig) - ig_g) / CR;
  s_mk += (t_mk - s_mk) * sm_c;  mk_i = (db2g(s_mk) - mk_g) / CR;
  og_i = (db2g(s_out - (has_v ? 0.25 * dm_a * sag_amt : 0)) * vg - out_g) / CR;
  // each slot: its drive (THICK pushes every stage harder), bias and slope, with its own drift
  // valve: HT sag; iron: core temperature; transistor: bias wander + heat; solid state: rail sag
  stk_p = 1 + 0.6 * thk_m;
  tb_h = 0.08 * min(1, heat / 0.25);
  kir = sk_of(1, s_dir) * stk_p * (1 + 0.08 * dm_a * dw_ir);                 // iron: core temperature
  ktr = sk_of(2, s_dtr) * stk_p;
  kss = sk_of(3, s_dss) * stk_p * (1 + 0.12 * dm_a * sag_amt);               // solid state: rail sag
  kva = sk_of(4, s_dva) * stk_p * (1 + 0.15 * dm_a * sag_amt);               // valve: HT sag
  btr = TR_B + dm_a * (0.05 * dw_tr + tb_h);                                 // transistor: bias wander + heat
  bva = vb + 0.10 * thk_m;
  k1 = r1 == 1 ? kir : r1 == 2 ? ktr : r1 == 3 ? kss : kva;  b1 = r1 == 2 ? btr : r1 == 4 ? bva : 0;
  k2 = r2 == 1 ? kir : r2 == 2 ? ktr : r2 == 3 ? kss : kva;  b2 = r2 == 2 ? btr : r2 == 4 ? bva : 0;
  k3 = r3 == 1 ? kir : r3 == 2 ? ktr : r3 == 3 ? kss : kva;  b3 = r3 == 2 ? btr : r3 == 4 ? bva : 0;
  k4 = r4 == 1 ? kir : r4 == 2 ? ktr : r4 == 3 ? kss : kva;  b4 = r4 == 2 ? btr : r4 == 4 ? bva : 0;
  l1 = dts(b1);  l2 = dts(b2);  l3 = dts(b3);  l4 = dts(b4);
  xik = XI_K * (1 + 0.8 * thk_m);
  // the compressor: feed-forward RMS, soft knee; an optical-style memory slows the release after long, heavy GR
  lv = g2db(sqrt(ms)) + 18;
  ov = lv - s_thr;
  sl_ = 1 - 1 / s_rat;
  tgr = ov <= -KNEE * 0.5 ? 0 : ov < KNEE * 0.5 ? -sl_ * sqr(ov + KNEE * 0.5) / (2 * KNEE) : -sl_ * ov;
  mem += (min(1, -gr / 8) - mem) * (1 - exp(-CR / (1.5 * srate)));          // TWEAK: builds over ~1.5 s
  ac = 1 - exp(-CR / (atk * 0.001 * age_a * srate));
  rc = 1 - exp(-CR / (rel * 0.001 * age_r * (1 + mem) * srate));
  gr += (tgr - gr) * (tgr < gr ? ac : rc);
  grmin = min(grmin, gr);
  cgi = (db2g(gr) - cg) / CR;
);
cr_n -= 1;
ig_g += ig_i;  out_g += og_i;  cg += cgi;
m_in += (t_in - m_in) * sw_c;  m_v += (t_v - m_v) * sw_c;  mk_g += mk_i;  mix_s += (mix / 100 - mix_s) * mix_c;
// a stage change: out of the stack (5 ms), swap at the dry point (the new stage starts from rest), back in
q1 != r1 || q2 != r2 || q3 != r3 || q4 != r4 ? (
  dk = max(dk - dk_c, 0);
  dk == 0 ? (
    q1 != r1 ? ( S1L.stage_clr(); S1R.stage_clr(); );  q2 != r2 ? ( S2L.stage_clr(); S2R.stage_clr(); );
    q3 != r3 ? ( S3L.stage_clr(); S3R.stage_clr(); );  q4 != r4 ? ( S4L.stage_clr(); S4R.stage_clr(); );
    r1 = q1;  r2 = q2;  r3 = q3;  r4 = q4;
  );
) : dk < 1 ? dk = min(dk + dk_c, 1);
stk_m = m_v * dk * dk * (3 - 2 * dk);
// each stage's own IN (12 ms), then each position takes its stage's fade
m_ir += (t_mir - m_ir) * sw_c;  m_tr += (t_mtr - m_tr) * sw_c;  m_ss += (t_mss - m_ss) * sw_c;  m_va += (t_mva - m_va) * sw_c;
m_ir < 0.00001 ? m_ir = 0;  m_tr < 0.00001 ? m_tr = 0;  m_ss < 0.00001 ? m_ss = 0;  m_va < 0.00001 ? m_va = 0;
m1 = r1 == 1 ? m_ir : r1 == 2 ? m_tr : r1 == 3 ? m_ss : m_va;  m2 = r2 == 1 ? m_ir : r2 == 2 ? m_tr : r2 == 3 ? m_ss : m_va;
m3 = r3 == 1 ? m_ir : r3 == 2 ? m_tr : r3 == 3 ? m_ss : m_va;  m4 = r4 == 1 ? m_ir : r4 == 2 ? m_tr : r4 == 3 ? m_ss : m_va;

// ---------- input transformer, INPUT GAIN ----------
xl = XIL.xfmr(spl0, xik) * ig_g;  xr = XIR.xfmr(spl1, xik) * ig_g;
// GUARD (the house input guard, as gfx-lab-input): eases hot sources down towards -18 dBFS average (~1 s, never boosts)
// and catches peaks above -6 dBFS (8:1, soft knee); its detectors always run, so the key crossfades (12 ms)
gd_m += ((guard >= 0.5) - gd_m) * sw_c;
gd_ms += (0.5 * (xl * xl + xr * xr) - gd_ms) * gd_msc;
gd_ag += ((gd_ms > 0.0159 ? 0.126 / sqrt(gd_ms) : 1) - gd_ag) * gd_agc;
gd_pk = max(abs(xl), abs(xr)) * gd_ag;
gd_env += (gd_pk - gd_env) * (gd_pk > gd_env ? gd_catt : gd_crel);
gd_ov = 20 * log10(max(gd_env, 0.000001)) + 6;
gd_cr = gd_ov <= -3 ? 0 : gd_ov >= 3 ? 0.875 * gd_ov : 0.875 * sqr(gd_ov + 3) / 12;
gd_m > 0.00001 ? ( gd_g = 1 + (gd_ag * db2g(-gd_cr) - 1) * gd_m;  xl *= gd_g;  xr *= gd_g; );

// ---------- the PREAMP STACK, oversampled (the dry path runs through the same filters, so PREAMP swaps cleanly) ----------
os_gate();
os_chg ? ( stk_coefs();  S1L.stage_clr(); S1R.stage_clr(); S2L.stage_clr(); S2R.stage_clr();
           S3L.stage_clr(); S3R.stage_clr(); S4L.stage_clr(); S4R.stage_clr(); );
UPL.os_up(xl);  UPR.os_up(xr);
stack(UPL.s0, UPR.s0);  a0 = pl;  c0 = pr;
os_f == 1 ? ( xl = a0;  xr = c0; ) : (
  stack(UPL.s1, UPR.s1);  a1 = pl;  c1 = pr;
  os_f == 2 ? ( xl = DNL.os_dn(a0, a1, 0, 0);  xr = DNR.os_dn(c0, c1, 0, 0); ) : (
    stack(UPL.s2, UPR.s2);  a2 = pl;  c2 = pr;
    stack(UPL.s3, UPR.s3);  a3 = pl;  c3 = pr;
    xl = DNL.os_dn(a0, a1, a2, a3);  xr = DNR.os_dn(c0, c1, c2, c3);
  );
);
os_gs = os_g * os_g * (3 - 2 * os_g);                                         // the OS swap's dip
xl *= os_gs;  xr *= os_gs;
heat += (max(abs(xl), abs(xr)) - heat) * heat_c;
thk_proc(xl, xr, thick >= 0.5);  xl = thk_l;  xr = thk_r;    // THICK, between the preamp and the compressor

// ---------- the compressor (detector on its input, linked stereo) ----------
ms += (max(xl * xl, xr * xr) - ms) * (rms_c + (rms_c2 - rms_c) * thk_m);
// MAKE-UP on the compressed path, MIX = parallel compression (the preamp's sound against its compressed copy), IN
yl = xl * cg * mk_g;  yr = xr * cg * mk_g;
yl = xl + (yl - xl) * mix_s;  yr = xr + (yr - xr) * mix_s;
yl = xl + (yl - xl) * m_in;  yr = xr + (yr - xr) * m_in;

// ---------- output transformer, LEVEL, the house output stage ----------
yl = XOL.xfmr(yl, XO_K) * out_g;  yr = XOR.xfmr(yr, XO_K) * out_g;
sag += (max(abs(yl), abs(yr)) - sag) * sag_c;
vul_acc += yl * yl;  vur_acc += yr * yr;  vu_n += 1;
yl = ostL.ost_band(yl);  yr = ostR.ost_band(yr);
ost_out(yl, yr);
spl0 = ost_l;  spl1 = ost_r;
by_out();
opk = max(opk, max(abs(spl0), abs(spl1)));                                   // OUT meter (peak)
// channels 3 and up: delayed by the latency (see @block)
xch_n > 0 ? (
  xch_k = 0;
  loop(xch_n,
    XCH[xch_k * 8192 + xch_w] = spl(xch_k + 2);
    spl(xch_k + 2) = XCH[xch_k * 8192 + ((xch_w - pdc_delay) & 8191)];
    xch_k += 1;
  );
  xch_w = (xch_w + 1) & 8191;
);

@gfx 1080 682
// GUI: two units stacked (as ACC24, warm orange accents), 1080 x 682 (design units).
//   unit 1 (0 - 322): header band 0 - 64; PREAMP STACK laid out at y 74 - 300, drawn 10 lower (INPUT GAIN + GUARD, four
//   stage modules at x 170 / 350 / 530 / 710 in stack order, PREAMP / THICK / HEATERS). A black rack gap 322 - 330.
//   unit 2 (330 - 682): band 330 - 374; COMPRESSOR 16 - 720 and OUTPUT 736 - 1064 (LEVEL with CLIP / DRIFT under it, then
//   the IN / OUT LED ladders; the GAIN REDUCTION LED row under THRESHOLD - trial, JG 28 Oct), laid out at y 316 - 596 and drawn 74 lower.
C_FACE = 0x2B2D2F;  C_HEAD = 0x1D1E20;  C_INK = 0xF1F0EB;  C_INK2 = 0xB9B8B2;  C_LINE = 0xC7BEB3;
C_YEL = 0xF2C230;  C_LCDBG = 0x0B0D0E;  C_LCDTX = 0xF2C26A;  C_CREAM = 0xF1E6C4;
C_ORG = 0xC4621C;  C_ORGL = 0xF2A25A;      // the warm orange accents (JG, 28 Oct 2026; ACC24 has green)
LK_AMB = 0xF2A41E;  LK_YEL = 0xF2C230;  lk_well = 0x050505;
VUS = 20000;                              // GUI memory: the faceplate grain, the VU needles

function col(h, a) (
  gfx_r = floor(h / 65536) / 255;  gfx_g = (floor(h / 256) % 256) / 255;  gfx_b = (h % 256) / 255;  gfx_a = a;
);
function shade(h, f) local(r, g, b) (
  r = min(255, floor(floor(h / 65536) * f));  g = min(255, floor((floor(h / 256) % 256) * f));
  b = min(255, floor((h % 256) * f));  r * 65536 + g * 256 + b;
);
function ui_mix(c1, c2, t) (
  floor(floor(c1 / 65536) * (1 - t) + floor(c2 / 65536) * t) * 65536 +
  floor((floor(c1 / 256) % 256) * (1 - t) + (floor(c2 / 256) % 256) * t) * 256 +
  floor((c1 % 256) * (1 - t) + (c2 % 256) * t);
);
function px(v) ( ox + v * sc; );
function py(v) ( oy + v * sc; );
function ps(v) ( v * sc; );
function u_rect(x, y, w, h) ( gfx_rect(px(x), py(y), ps(w), ps(h), 1); );
function text_c(x, y, str) local(w, h) ( gfx_measurestr(str, w, h);  gfx_x = x - w * 0.5;  gfx_y = y - h * 0.5;  gfx_drawstr(str); );
function text_l(x, y, str) local(w, h) ( gfx_measurestr(str, w, h);  gfx_x = x;  gfx_y = y - h * 0.5;  gfx_drawstr(str); );
function rivet(x, y) (
  col(0x55585C, 1);  gfx_circle(px(x), py(y), ps(3.5), 1, 1);
  col(0xFFFFFF, 0.35);  gfx_circle(px(x) - ps(1), py(y) - ps(1), ps(1.2), 1, 1);
  col(0x000000, 0.6);  gfx_line(px(x) - ps(2), py(y), px(x) + ps(2), py(y), 1);
);
// an outlined section: the title (and lamps) sit in gaps in the top line
// one rounded corner of an outline, anti-aliased, in device pixels: (cx, cy) the arc's centre, ra the outer radius,
// th the line width, sx / sy which way the corner faces (-1 = left / top, 1 = right / bottom)
function ocorner(cx, cy, ra, th, sx, sy) local(i, j, d, c) (
  j = 0;
  loop(ra,
    i = 0;
    loop(ra,
      d = sqrt(sqr(i + 0.5) + sqr(j + 0.5));
      c = max(0, min(1, min(ra - d + 0.5, d - (ra - th) + 0.5)));
      c > 0 ? ( gfx_a = 0.85 * c;  gfx_rect(sx < 0 ? cx - i - 1 : cx + i, sy < 0 ? cy - j - 1 : cy + j, 1, 1, 1); );
      i += 1;
    );
    j += 1;
  );
);
// an outlined section: whole device pixels throughout so the lines and the corners meet exactly; the title
// (and lamps, gx0 - gx1) sit in gaps in the top line
function box(x, y, w, h, title, gx0, gx1) local(tw, th, L, R, T, B, ra, lw, g0, g1) (
  gfx_setfont(4);  gfx_measurestr(title, tw, th);
  L = floor(px(x) + 0.5);  R = floor(px(x + w) + 0.5);  T = floor(py(y) + 0.5);  B = floor(py(y + h) + 0.5);
  ra = floor(ps(7) + 0.5);  lw = max(1, floor(ps(1.5) + 0.5));
  g0 = floor(px(x + w * 0.5) - tw * 0.5 - ps(8) + 0.5);  g1 = floor(px(x + w * 0.5) + tw * 0.5 + ps(8) + 0.5);
  col(C_LINE, 0.85);
  gfx_rect(L + ra, T, g0 - (L + ra), lw, 1);
  gx0 > 0 ? ( gfx_rect(g1, T, floor(px(gx0) + 0.5) - g1, lw, 1);  gfx_rect(floor(px(gx1) + 0.5), T, R - ra - floor(px(gx1) + 0.5), lw, 1); )
          : gfx_rect(g1, T, R - ra - g1, lw, 1);
  gfx_rect(L + ra, B - lw, R - L - 2 * ra, lw, 1);
  gfx_rect(L, T + ra, lw, B - T - 2 * ra, 1);  gfx_rect(R - lw, T + ra, lw, B - T - 2 * ra, 1);
  ocorner(L + ra, T + ra, ra, lw, -1, -1);  ocorner(R - ra, T + ra, ra, lw, 1, -1);
  ocorner(L + ra, B - ra, ra, lw, -1, 1);   ocorner(R - ra, B - ra, ra, lw, 1, 1);
  col(C_INK, 1);  text_c(px(x + w * 0.5), T + lw * 0.5, title);
);
function fmtv(v, fmt) (
  fmt == 1 ? sprintf(#kv, "%+.1f dBu", v) :
  fmt == 2 ? sprintf(#kv, "%+.1f dB", v) :
  fmt == 3 ? sprintf(#kv, "%.1f : 1", v) :
  fmt == 4 ? sprintf(#kv, v < 10 ? "%.1f ms" : "%d ms", v) :
  fmt == 5 ? ( v < 1000 ? sprintf(#kv, "%d ms", v) : sprintf(#kv, "%.2f s", v / 1000); ) :
  fmt == 7 ? sprintf(#kv, "%d %%", v) :
             sprintf(#kv, "%.2f", v);
  #kv;
);
function hover_tag(x, y, str) local(w, h) (
  gfx_setfont(3);  gfx_measurestr(str, w, h);
  col(0x000000, 0.92);  gfx_rect(x - w * 0.5 - ps(6), y - h * 0.5 - ps(3), w + ps(12), h + ps(6), 1);
  col(C_LCDTX, 1);  text_c(x, y, str);
);
// a filled quad with soft edges (the pointer stripe)
function quad(ax, ay, bx, by, hw) local(dx, dy, l) (
  l = sqrt(sqr(bx - ax) + sqr(by - ay));  dx = -(by - ay) / l * hw;  dy = (bx - ax) / l * hw;
  gfx_triangle(ax + dx, ay + dy, bx + dx, by + dy, bx - dx, by - dy, ax - dx, ay - dy);
);
// a scale mark: a short white tick at t (0 - 1) and, if str is set, its number
function smark(cx, cy, r, t, str) local(a, sa, ca) (
  a = -0.75 * $pi + t * 1.5 * $pi;  sa = sin(a);  ca = cos(a);
  col(C_INK, 0.9);  gfx_line(px(cx + sa * (r + 4)), py(cy - ca * (r + 4)), px(cx + sa * (r + 8)), py(cy - ca * (r + 8)), 1);
  strlen(str) ? ( gfx_setfont(5);  col(C_INK, 1);  text_c(px(cx + sa * (r + 17)), py(cy - ca * (r + 16)), str); );
);
function lt(v, vmin, vmax) ( log(v / vmin) / log(vmax / vmin); );       // where v sits on a log knob
// Pointer knob: a black knurled skirt, a black cap, a yellow stripe the full radius. klog = 1 before a call: the
// travel is logarithmic. The label sits on the row's common line (klab_y), coloured kcol (white, or yellow for the
// key filters).
function kn(cx, cy, r, idx, vmin, vmax, def, lbl, fmt) local(x, y, rr, v, t, hov, now, a, j, lg, b)
(
  lg = klog;  klog = 0;
  x = px(cx);  y = py(cy);  rr = ps(r);
  hov = sqr(mouse_x - x) + sqr(mouse_y - y) <= sqr(rr * 1.25);
  v = max(vmin, min(vmax, slider(idx)));
  t = lg ? lt(v, vmin, vmax) : (v - vmin) / (vmax - vmin);
  click && hov && !drag_idx ? (
    now = time_precise();
    (mouse_cap & 4) || (last_click_idx == idx && now - last_click_t < 0.35) ? (
      slider(idx) = def;  param_touched(idx);  drag_idx = 0;
    ) : ( drag_idx = idx;  drag_y = mouse_y;  drag_t = t; );
    last_click_idx = idx;  last_click_t = now;
  );
  hov && mouse_wheel != 0 && !drag_idx ? (
    t = max(0, min(1, t + mouse_wheel / 120 * ((mouse_cap & 8) ? 0.005 : 0.03)));
    v = lg ? vmin * (vmax / vmin) ^ t : vmin + t * (vmax - vmin);
    v = v >= 100 ? floor(v + 0.5) : floor(v * 100 + 0.5) / 100;
    v != slider(idx) ? ( slider(idx) = v;  param_touched(idx); );
    mouse_wheel = 0;
  );
  drag_idx == idx ? (
    t = max(0, min(1, drag_t + (drag_y - mouse_y) / ps((mouse_cap & 8) ? 1100 : 220)));
    v = lg ? vmin * (vmax / vmin) ^ t : vmin + t * (vmax - vmin);
    v = v >= 100 ? floor(v + 0.5) : lg ? floor(v * 100 + 0.5) / 100 : floor(v * 10 + 0.5) / 10;
    v = max(vmin, min(vmax, v));
    v != slider(idx) ? ( slider(idx) = v;  param_touched(idx); );
  );
  v = max(vmin, min(vmax, slider(idx)));
  t = lg ? lt(v, vmin, vmax) : (v - vmin) / (vmax - vmin);
  a = -0.75 * $pi + t * 1.5 * $pi;
  col(0x000000, 0.5);  gfx_circle(x + ps(1.5), y + ps(2.5), rr, 1, 1);                     // shadow
  col(0x0A0A0A, 1);  gfx_circle(x, y, rr, 1, 1);                                          // skirt
  col(0x2A2A2A, 1);  j = 0;                                                               // knurl
  loop(36, b = j / 36 * 2 * $pi;  gfx_line(x + sin(b) * rr * 0.84, y - cos(b) * rr * 0.84, x + sin(b) * (rr - 1), y - cos(b) * (rr - 1), 1);  j += 1; );
  col(0x1D1D1E, 1);  gfx_circle(x, y, rr * 0.78, 1, 1);                                   // cap
  col(0xFFFFFF, 0.10);  gfx_arc(x, y, rr * 0.72, -1.6, -0.3, 1);                          // one soft highlight
  col(0x3A3A3C, 1);  gfx_circle(x, y, rr, 0, 1);
  col(C_YEL, 1);  quad(x + sin(a) * rr * 0.18, y - cos(a) * rr * 0.18, x + sin(a) * rr * 0.97, y - cos(a) * rr * 0.97, ps(r >= 24 ? 1.7 : 1.4));
  gfx_setfont(6);  col(kcol ? kcol : C_INK, 1);  kcol = 0;
  text_c(x, py(klab_y), lbl);
  hov || drag_idx == idx ? hover_tag(x, y - rr - ps(18), fmtv(v, fmt));
);
// ---------- keys ----------
function ui_rrs(x, y, w, h, r) local(i, d, ins) (
  x = floor(x + 0.5); y = floor(y + 0.5); w = floor(w + 0.5); h = floor(h + 0.5);
  r = min(floor(r + 0.5), floor(min(w, h) * 0.5));
  i = 0;
  loop(r,
    d = r - i - 0.5; ins = floor(r - sqrt(max(r * r - d * d, 0)) + 0.5);
    gfx_rect(x + ins, y + i, w - 2 * ins, 1);  gfx_rect(x + ins, y + h - 1 - i, w - 2 * ins, 1);
    i += 1;
  );
  gfx_rect(x, y + r, w, h - 2 * r);
);
function lk_rr(x, y, w, h, r) ( ui_rrs(px(x), py(y), ps(w), ps(h), ps(r)); );
function ui_keytext(cx, cy, str) local(w, h) (
  gfx_measurestr(str, w, h); gfx_x = floor(cx - w * 0.5 + 0.5); gfx_y = floor(cy - h * 0.58 + 0.5); gfx_drawstr(str);
);
// house lamp key (IN, and the preset bar)
function lk_key(x, y, w, h, on, c, str) local(hov, hit, k, lens, dn, i, t, dx, dy) (
  hov = mouse_x >= px(x) && mouse_x < px(x + w) && mouse_y >= py(y) && mouse_y < py(y + h);
  hit = click && hov && !drag_idx;
  dn = hov && lmb ? 1 : 0;
  k = min(w / 54, h / 40);
  lens = shade(ui_mix(c, 0xCFC9BC, 0.5), 0.76);
  on ? lens = c;
  on ? (
    col(c, 0.10); lk_rr(x - 9 * k, y - 9 * k, w + 18 * k, h + 18 * k, 10 * k);
    col(c, 0.18); lk_rr(x - 6 * k, y - 6 * k, w + 12 * k, h + 12 * k, 8 * k);
  );
  col(lk_well, 1);           lk_rr(x - 4 * k, y - 4 * k, w + 8 * k, h + 8 * k, 5 * k);
  col(shade(lens, 0.55), 1); lk_rr(x, y + 1 / sc, w, h, 4 * k);
  y += (dn - 1) / sc;
  on ? (
    col(lens, 1); lk_rr(x, y, w, h - 1 / sc, 4 * k);
    i = 1;
    loop(4,
      t = 0.07 * i * (1 + 0.6 * max(1 - k, 0));
      dx = (i == 1 ? 3 : i == 2 ? 6 : i == 3 ? 10 : 14) * k;
      dy = (i == 1 ? 2 : i == 2 ? 4 : i == 3 ? 7 : 9) * k;
      col(ui_mix(c, 0xFFFFFF, t), 1); lk_rr(x + dx, y + dy, w - 2 * dx, h - 1 / sc - 2 * dy, 4 * k);
      i += 1;
    );
  ) : (
    col(shade(lens, 0.62), 1); lk_rr(x, y, w, h - 1 / sc, 4 * k);
    col(shade(lens, 0.78), 1); lk_rr(x + 2 * k, y + 2 * k, w - 4 * k, h - 5 * k, 4 * k);
    col(shade(lens, 0.92), 1); lk_rr(x + 5 * k, y + 4 * k, w - 10 * k, h - 10 * k, 4 * k);
    col(lens, 1);              lk_rr(x + 9 * k, y + 7 * k, w - 18 * k, h - 17 * k, 4 * k);
  );
  col(0xFFFFFF, on ? 0.45 : 0.22);  gfx_rect(px(x + 4 * k), py(y), ps(w - 8 * k), max(1, ps(1.5)));
  hov && !dn ? ( col(0xFFFFFF, 0.07); lk_rr(x, y, w, h - 1 / sc, 4 * k); );
  gfx_setfont(2);  col(shade(c, on ? 0.30 : 0.17), 1);
  ui_keytext(px(x + w * 0.5), py(y + h * 0.5), str);
  hit;
);
// square white push-button with an amber LED (the selector keys): pressed in and lit when on
function wk_key(x, y, w, h, on, str) local(hov, hit, b, dn) (
  hov = mouse_x >= px(x) && mouse_x < px(x + w) && mouse_y >= py(y) && mouse_y < py(y + h);
  hit = click && hov && !drag_idx;
  b = 1.6;  dn = on ? 0 : 1.6;
  col(0x000000, 0.5);  u_rect(x + 1, y + 2, w, h);
  col(0x050505, 1);  u_rect(x, y, w, h);
  col(on ? 0xEDEAE0 : 0xBDBAB0, 1);  u_rect(x + b, y + b + dn, w - 2 * b, h - 2 * b - dn);
  on ? ( col(0xFFFFFF, 0.6);  u_rect(x + b, y + b, w - 2 * b, 1);  col(0x000000, 0.15);  u_rect(x + b, y + h - b - 2, w - 2 * b, 2); )
     : ( col(0x000000, 0.3);  u_rect(x + b, y + b + dn, w - 2 * b, 1.5); );
  hov ? ( col(0xFFFFFF, 0.1);  u_rect(x + b, y + b + dn, w - 2 * b, h - 2 * b - dn); );
  on ? ( col(0xFFB030, 0.35);  gfx_circle(px(x + 10), py(y + h * 0.5 + dn * 0.5), ps(5), 1, 1); );
  col(on ? 0xFFB030 : 0x6B5A3C, 1);  gfx_circle(px(x + 10), py(y + h * 0.5 + dn * 0.5), ps(2.8), 1, 1);
  gfx_setfont(2);  col(on ? 0x22201C : 0x4E4A44, 1);
  ui_keytext(px(x + w * 0.5 + 6), py(y + h * 0.5 + dn * 0.5), str);
  hit;
);
// a small plain square grey push-button (THICK, DRIFT); its red LED sits to its right and its name is printed on
// the faceplate under the pair. (x, y) = the button's top left; returns 1 when the button is clicked
function sq_key(x, y, on, lbl) local(hov, hit, s, b, dn) (
  s = 22;  b = 2;  dn = on ? 1.5 : 0;
  hov = mouse_x >= px(x) && mouse_x < px(x + s) && mouse_y >= py(y) && mouse_y < py(y + s);
  hit = click && hov && !drag_idx;
  col(0x000000, 0.5);  u_rect(x + 1, y + 2, s, s);
  col(0x050505, 1);  u_rect(x, y, s, s);                                       // the well
  col(on ? 0x8A8C90 : 0x9C9EA2, 1);  u_rect(x + b, y + b + dn, s - 2 * b, s - 2 * b - dn);   // the grey cap
  !on ? ( col(0xFFFFFF, 0.28);  u_rect(x + b, y + b, s - 2 * b, 1);
          col(0x000000, 0.28);  u_rect(x + b, y + s - b - 2, s - 2 * b, 2); )
      : ( col(0x000000, 0.35);  u_rect(x + b, y + b + dn, s - 2 * b, 1.5); );
  hov ? ( col(0xFFFFFF, 0.08);  u_rect(x + b, y + b + dn, s - 2 * b, s - 2 * b - dn); );
  // the LED, to the right
  col(0x000000, 1);  gfx_circle(px(x + s + 12), py(y + s * 0.5), ps(5.2), 1, 1);
  col(on ? 0xFF2A1A : 0x4A1410, 1);  gfx_circle(px(x + s + 12), py(y + s * 0.5), ps(3.8), 1, 1);
  on ? ( col(0xFF3A2A, 0.3);  gfx_circle(px(x + s + 12), py(y + s * 0.5), ps(8), 1, 1);
         col(0xFFFFFF, 0.55);  gfx_circle(px(x + s + 11), py(y + s * 0.5 - 1), ps(1.2), 1, 1); );
  // the label, printed on the faceplate
  gfx_setfont(7);  col(C_INK, 1);  text_c(px(x + (s + 17) * 0.5), py(y + s + 12), lbl);
  hit;
);
// a round LED lamp
function lamp(x, y, c, on) local(k) (
  k = lamp_k > 0 ? lamp_k : 1;  lamp_k = 0;                 // lamp_k before a call: size (1 = standard)
  col(0x000000, 1);  gfx_circle(px(x), py(y), ps(6 * k), 1, 1);
  col(on ? c : shade(c, 0.28), 1);  gfx_circle(px(x), py(y), ps(4.6 * k), 1, 1);
  on ? ( col(c, 0.28);  gfx_circle(px(x), py(y), ps(9 * k), 1, 1);  col(0xFFFFFF, 0.55);  gfx_circle(px(x - 1.5 * k), py(y - 1.5 * k), ps(1.4 * k), 1, 1); );
);
// ---------- LED ladders ----------
// one LED: a small rounded block, lit or dim
function led(x, y, w, h, c, on) (
  col(0x000000, 1);  u_rect(x - 1, y - 1, w + 2, h + 2);
  col(on ? c : shade(c, 0.22), 1);  u_rect(x, y, w, h);
  on ? ( col(0xFFFFFF, 0.3);  u_rect(x + 1, y + 1, w - 2, 1); );
);
// level ladder, house: -42 .. +3 dBFS in 3 dB steps (16 LEDs), green / yellow from -6 / red from 0;
// a held peak LED (1.2 s, then 0.6 dB a frame); slot = which hold (in GUI memory)
function ladder(x, y, v, slot) local(j, d, c, pk) (
  now_t = time_precise();
  v > VUS[slot] ? ( VUS[slot] = v;  VUS[slot + 1] = now_t; ) :
    now_t - VUS[slot + 1] > 1.2 ? VUS[slot] = max(v, VUS[slot] - 0.6);
  pk = VUS[slot];
  j = 0;
  loop(16,
    d = -42 + j * 3;  c = d >= 0 ? 0xFF3A2A : d >= -6 ? 0xFFC81E : 0x3CE05A;
    led(x + j * 11, y, 8, 12, c, v >= d || (pk >= d && pk < d + 3));
    j += 1;
  );
);

// vertical LED ladder (the house LED ladder meter): 15 LEDs, -42 .. 0 dBFS in 3 dB steps, green / amber from -9 /
// red at 0, a floating peak held 1.2 s then falling 0.6 dB a frame; slot = its hold (GUI memory); a click clears holds
function vladder(x, y, w, h, v, slot) local(j, d, c, pk, sh, on) (
  now_t = time_precise();
  click && mouse_x >= px(x - 4) && mouse_x < px(x + w + 4) && mouse_y >= py(y) && mouse_y < py(y + h) ? lad_clr = now_t;
  VUS[slot + 1] < lad_clr ? ( VUS[slot] = -100;  VUS[slot + 1] = lad_clr; );
  v > VUS[slot] ? ( VUS[slot] = v;  VUS[slot + 1] = now_t; ) :
    now_t - VUS[slot + 1] > 1.2 ? VUS[slot] = max(v, VUS[slot] - 0.6);
  pk = VUS[slot];
  col(0x000000, 1);  u_rect(x - 3, y - 3, w + 6, h + 6);
  col(0x161617, 1);  u_rect(x - 1, y - 1, w + 2, h + 2);
  sh = h / 15;
  j = 0;
  loop(15,
    d = -42 + j * 3;  c = d >= 0 ? 0xFF3A2A : d >= -9 ? 0xFFC81E : 0x3CE05A;
    on = v >= d || (pk >= d && pk < d + 3 && pk > -42);
    on ? ( col(c, 0.3);  u_rect(x - 1, y + h - (j + 1) * sh - 1, w + 2, sh + 1); );
    col(on ? c : shade(c, 0.2), 1);  u_rect(x, y + h - (j + 1) * sh + 1, w, sh - 1.5);
    on ? ( col(0xFFFFFF, 0.25);  u_rect(x + 1, y + h - (j + 1) * sh + 1, w - 2, 1); );
    j += 1;
  );
);

function vu(x, y, w, h, val, val2, grm, lbl, slot) local(nn, vv, cx, cyp, R, j, d, t, a, xx, yy, n, lin, sp, ti, to, tl, nl)
(
  vg_spill(px(x - 3), py(y - 3), ps(w + 6), ps(h + 6), 1);              // backlit (gfx-glow)
  col(0x2A2F2B, 1);  u_rect(x - 3, y - 3, w + 6, h + 6);
  vg_glow(px(x), py(y), ps(w), ps(h), 1);
  cx = x + w * 0.5;
  h < 80 ? ( cyp = y + h + 90;  R = h + 78;  sp = 0.42;  ti = R - 17;  to = R - 9;  tl = R + 1;  nl = R - 11; )   // short face: flat arc, numbers above the ticks
         : ( cyp = y + h + 34;  R = h + 14;  sp = 0.78;  ti = R - 10;  to = R;  tl = R - 20;  nl = R - 2; );
  // scale: angle from -sp to +sp rad
  j = 0;
  loop(grm ? 5 : 10,
    grm ? ( d = j == 0 ? 0 : j == 1 ? 3 : j == 2 ? 6 : j == 3 ? 10 : 20;  t = 1 - sqrt(d / 20); ) :
          ( d = j == 0 ? -20 : j == 1 ? -10 : j == 2 ? -7 : j == 3 ? -5 : j == 4 ? -3 : j == 5 ? -1 : j == 6 ? 0 : j == 7 ? 1 : j == 8 ? 2 : 3;
            lin = 10 ^ (d / 20);  t = (lin - 0.1) / (1.4125 - 0.1); );
    a = -sp + t * 2 * sp;
    col(!grm && d > 0 ? 0xC0302A : 0x1E1E1A, 1);
    gfx_line(px(cx + sin(a) * ti), py(cyp - cos(a) * ti), px(cx + sin(a) * to), py(cyp - cos(a) * to), 1);
    gfx_setfont(5);
    grm ? sprintf(#vl, "%d", d) : sprintf(#vl, d > 0 ? "+%d" : "%d", d);
    (grm || j == 0 || j == 1 || (j == 3 && h >= 80) || j == 6 || j == 9) ? text_c(px(cx + sin(a) * tl), py(cyp - cos(a) * tl), #vl);
    j += 1;
  );
  !grm ? ( col(0xC0302A, 1);  n = 0;                                   // the red arc above 0 VU
    loop(20, t = (1 + n / 20 * 0.4125 - 0.1) / 1.3125;  a = -sp + t * 2 * sp;  gfx_rect(px(cx + sin(a) * R) - 1, py(cyp - cos(a) * R) - 1, ps(2), ps(2), 1);  n += 1; ); );
  gfx_setfont(6);  col(0x1E1E1A, 1);  text_c(px(cx), py(y + h - 14), lbl);
  nn = 0;                                   // GR: one needle; OUTPUT: left (black) and right (red)
  loop(grm ? 1 : 2,
  // the needle (spring ballistics, ~300 ms)
  vv = nn ? val2 : val;
  grm ? t = 1 - sqrt(min(20, max(0, -vv)) / 20) :
        ( lin = 10 ^ (max(-30, min(4, vv)) / 20);  t = max(-0.04, min(1.04, (lin - 0.1) / 1.3125)); );
  VUS[(slot + nn) * 2 + 1] += ((t - VUS[(slot + nn) * 2]) * 0.24 - VUS[(slot + nn) * 2 + 1] * 0.5);
  VUS[(slot + nn) * 2] += VUS[(slot + nn) * 2 + 1];
  a = -sp + max(-0.06, min(1.06, VUS[(slot + nn) * 2])) * 2 * sp;
  gfx_x = 0;  col(nn ? 0xB0281E : 0x111111, 1);
  xx = cx + sin(a) * nl;  yy = cyp - cos(a) * nl;
  n = (cyp - (y + h - 4)) / cos(a);                                   // the needle starts where it leaves the face's foot
  gfx_line(px(cx + sin(a) * n), py(cyp - cos(a) * n), px(xx), py(yy), 1);
  nn += 1;
  );
  col(0x2A2F2B, 1);  u_rect(x, y + h - 4, w, 4);
);


PRESET_MENU = "Init|Valve Warmth DI|Rich Bass Guitar|Vocal Tube Fatten|Drum Bus Crunch|Synth Thickening|Acoustic Warmth|Master Bus Glue|Saturated Parallel|Subtle Colour|Console Edge|Hot Source Tamer";
// ---------- house preset bar: [PRESETS][<][>][LCD] ----------
function pb_count(menu) local(k, n) ( n = 1;  k = 0;  loop(strlen(menu), str_getchar(menu, k) == 124 ? n += 1;  k += 1; );  n; );
function pb_item(menu, i, dst) local(k, k0, n, c, len) (
  strcpy(dst, "");  len = strlen(menu);  k = 0;  k0 = 0;  n = 1;
  loop(len + 1,
    c = k < len ? str_getchar(menu, k) : 124;
    c == 124 ? ( n == i ? strcpy_substr(dst, menu, k0, k - k0);  n += 1;  k0 = k + 1; );
    k += 1;
  );
  dst;
);
function lcd(x, y, w, h, str) local(tw, th, gy) (
  col(0x2A2B2D, 1);  u_rect(x - 2, y - 2, w + 4, h + 4);
  col(0x000000, 1);  u_rect(x, y, w, h);
  col(C_LCDBG, 1);   u_rect(x + 3, y + 3, w - 6, h - 6);
  gfx_setfont(8);  gfx_measurestr(str, tw, th);  gy = py(y + h * 0.5) - th * 0.5;
  col(C_LCDTX, 0.22);  gfx_x = px(x + 10) - 1;  gfx_y = gy;  gfx_drawstr(str);  gfx_x = px(x + 10) + 1;  gfx_y = gy;  gfx_drawstr(str);
  col(C_LCDTX, 1);  gfx_x = px(x + 10);  gfx_y = gy;  gfx_drawstr(str);
);
function pb_tri(cx, cy, s, dir) ( gfx_triangle(px(cx + dir * s), py(cy), px(cx - dir * s), py(cy - s), px(cx - dir * s), py(cy + s)); );
function preset_bar(x, y, h, lw, cur, menu) local(n, sel, open, lx, i) (
  n = pb_count(menu);  sel = 0;  open = 0;
  lk_key(x, y + 3, 92, h - 6, 0, 0xD8DCD2, "PRESETS") ? open = 1;
  lk_key(x + 102, y + 3, 38, h - 6, 0, 0xD8DCD2, "") ? ( sel = cur <= 1 || cur > n ? n : cur - 1; );
  lk_key(x + 150, y + 3, 38, h - 6, 0, 0xD8DCD2, "") ? ( sel = cur >= n || cur < 1 ? 1 : cur + 1; );
  col(0x1A1A1A, 1);  pb_tri(x + 121, y + h * 0.5, 5, -1);  pb_tri(x + 169, y + h * 0.5, 5, 1);
  lx = x + 202;
  cur >= 1 && cur <= n ? pb_item(menu, cur, #pb_nm) : strcpy(#pb_nm, "--");
  lcd(lx, y, lw, h, #pb_nm);
  click && mouse_x >= px(lx) && mouse_x < px(lx + lw) && mouse_y >= py(y) && mouse_y < py(y + h) ? open = 1;
  open ? (
    strcpy(#pb_m, "");  i = 1;
    loop(n, i == cur ? strcat(#pb_m, "!");  strcat(#pb_m, pb_item(menu, i, #pb_t));  strcat(#pb_m, "|");  i += 1; );
    strcat(#pb_m, "Reset all to defaults");
    gfx_x = px(x);  gfx_y = py(y + h);  i = gfx_showmenu(#pb_m);  i > 0 ? sel = i;
  );
  sel;
);

// ---------- the preamp stages: fixed modules IRON / TRANSISTOR / SOLID STATE / VALVE, moved along the stack by their < > keys ----------
function st_col(t) ( t == 1 ? 0xC9774A : t == 2 ? 0x7FC27A : t == 3 ? 0x7FB2E6 : 0xF2B24A; );
// the stage order (slider 24) for the panel: its own copy of the decoder (the audio side has ord_dec)
function gord_nth(n) local(i, r) (
  r = 0;  i = 1;
  loop(4, (i == 1 ? gu1 : i == 2 ? gu2 : i == 3 ? gu3 : gu4) == 0 ? ( n == 0 && r == 0 ? r = i;  n -= 1; );  i += 1; );
  r == 1 ? gu1 = 1 : r == 2 ? gu2 = 1 : r == 3 ? gu3 = 1 : gu4 = 1;
  r;
);
function gord_dec(c) (
  c = max(0, min(23, c | 0));  gu1 = gu2 = gu3 = gu4 = 0;
  gq1 = gord_nth(floor(c / 6));  gq2 = gord_nth(floor((c % 6) / 2));  gq3 = gord_nth(c % 2);  gq4 = gord_nth(0);
);
// how many of the stages not yet placed come before t
function gord_rank(t) local(i, r) (
  r = 0;  i = 1;
  loop(t - 1, (i == 1 ? gu1 : i == 2 ? gu2 : i == 3 ? gu3 : gu4) == 0 ? r += 1;  i += 1; );
  t == 1 ? gu1 = 1 : t == 2 ? gu2 = 1 : t == 3 ? gu3 = 1 : gu4 = 1;
  r;
);
function gord_enc(a, b, c) ( gu1 = gu2 = gu3 = gu4 = 0;  gord_rank(a) * 6 + gord_rank(b) * 2 + gord_rank(c); );
// swap the stages at positions p and p + 1 (1 - 3)
function gord_swap(p) local(a, b, c, d, t) (
  a = gq1;  b = gq2;  c = gq3;  d = gq4;
  p == 1 ? ( t = a;  a = b;  b = t; ) : p == 2 ? ( t = b;  b = c;  c = t; ) : ( t = c;  c = d;  d = t; );
  slider(24) = gord_enc(a, b, c);  param_touched(24);
);
function gord_pos(t) ( gq1 == t ? 1 : gq2 == t ? 2 : gq3 == t ? 3 : 4; );
// a small < or > key (dir -1 / 1); dimmed and dead at the end of the stack
function mv_key(x, y, dir, live) local(hit) (
  hit = lk_key(x, y, 40, 22, 0, 0xD8DCD2, "") && live;
  col(0x1A1A1A, live ? 1 : 0.3);  pb_tri(x + 20, y + 10, 4.5, dir);
  hit;
);
// the stage's name in a dark recessed box (its colour when in, dim when out); a click switches the stage in / out
function st_box(x, y, w, h, t, on, lbl) local(hov, i) (
  hov = mouse_x >= px(x) && mouse_x < px(x + w) && mouse_y >= py(y) && mouse_y < py(y + h);
  col(0x000000, 0.13);  i = 0;  loop(4, u_rect(x + 2 + i * 1.3, y + 3 + i * 1.6, w + i * 0.5, h + i * 0.5);  i += 1; );
  col(0x111213, 1);  u_rect(x, y, w, h);
  col(0x000000, 1);  u_rect(x, y, w, 2);  u_rect(x, y, 2, h);                  // recessed: shaded top and left
  col(0x3A3B3E, 1);  u_rect(x, y + h - 1, w, 1);  u_rect(x + w - 1, y, 1, h);
  hov ? ( col(0xFFFFFF, 0.06);  u_rect(x + 2, y + 2, w - 3, h - 3); );
  gfx_setfont(6);  col(on ? st_col(t) : 0x6E6E6A, 1);
  text_c(px(x + w * 0.5), py(y + h * 0.5), lbl);
  click && hov && !drag_idx;
);
// one stage module at x (its place in the stack, eased): its lamp key (lit = in), DRIVE, < >
function stage_mod(x, t, lbl, onidx, didx, def) local(cx, on, p) (
  cx = x + 84;  on = slider(onidx) >= 0.5;  p = gord_pos(t);
  col(0x323437, 1);  u_rect(x, 94, 168, 190);
  col(0x000000, 0.35);  u_rect(x, 94, 168, 1.5);  u_rect(x, 94, 1.5, 190);
  col(0xFFFFFF, 0.05);  u_rect(x, 282.5, 168, 1.5);  u_rect(x + 166.5, 94, 1.5, 190);
  st_box(x + 20, 104, 128, 30, t, on, lbl) ? ( slider(onidx) = on ? 0 : 1;  param_touched(onidx); );
  col(st_col(t), on ? 1 : 0.3);  u_rect(x + 20, 138, 128, 3);
  klab_y = 238;
  smark(cx, 192, 26, 0, "0");  smark(cx, 192, 26, 0.5, "50");  smark(cx, 192, 26, 1, "100");
  smark(cx, 192, 26, 0.25, "");  smark(cx, 192, 26, 0.75, "");
  kn(cx, 192, 26, didx, 0, 100, def, "DRIVE", 7);
  !on || v_on < 0.5 ? ( col(0x323437, 0.6);  gfx_circle(px(cx), py(192), ps(27), 1, 1); );
  mv_key(x + 38, 252, -1, p > 1) ? gord_swap(p - 1);
  mv_key(x + 90, 252, 1, p < 4) ? gord_swap(p);
);
// where each stage's module sits: eased towards its place in the stack (about 0.15 s), so a move is seen
function mod_x(t) local(tx) (
  tx = 170 + (gord_pos(t) - 1) * 180;
  !mx_ok ? VUS[90 + t] = tx;
  VUS[90 + t] += (tx - VUS[90 + t]) * 0.35;  abs(tx - VUS[90 + t]) < 0.5 ? VUS[90 + t] = tx;
  VUS[90 + t];
);

// ---------- frame setup ----------
PNL_W = 1080;  PNL_H = 682;
g_ret = gfx_ext_retina > 1 ? gfx_ext_retina : 1;
g_want = ui_sz == 1 ? 0.85 : ui_sz == 2 ? 1.3 : 1;
sc = g_ret * max(min(g_want, min(gfx_w / (PNL_W * g_ret), gfx_h / (PNL_H * g_ret))), 0.5);
ox = 0;  oy = 0;                              // (the OS and BYPASS keys draw from the top left)
lmb = mouse_cap & 1;
click = lmb && !last_lmb;
kcol = 0;  klog = 0;

gfx_setfont(1, "Trebuchet MS", ps(30), 'b');
gfx_setfont(10, "Trebuchet MS", ps(12), 'b');
gfx_setfont(2, "Trebuchet MS", ps(12), 'b');
gfx_setfont(3, "Verdana", ps(13), 'b');
gfx_setfont(4, "Trebuchet MS", ps(15), 'b');
gfx_setfont(5, "Trebuchet MS", ps(11), 'b');
gfx_setfont(6, "Trebuchet MS", ps(13), 'b');
gfx_setfont(7, "Trebuchet MS", ps(10), 'b');
gfx_setfont(8, "Courier New", ps(19.7), 'b');

// ---------- the faceplates: two units stacked (JG, 28 Oct 2026, as ACC24) ----------
// unit 1 (0 - 322): VAL60 header band (0 - 64), PREAMP STACK; a black rack gap 322 - 330; unit 2 (330 - 682): its own
// band (330 - 374), COMPRESSOR and OUTPUT. Each top bar ends in a warm orange rule with an orange tab beside the unit's
// name, with room above and below it (JG).
col(0x050505, 1);  gfx_rect(0, 0, gfx_w, gfx_h, 1);
col(C_FACE, 1);  u_rect(0, 0, PNL_W, 322);  u_rect(0, 330, PNL_W, 352);
!grain_ok ? (
  g_j = 0;  loop(1800, VUS[100 + g_j * 3] = rand(PNL_W);  VUS[101 + g_j * 3] = rand(PNL_H);  VUS[102 + g_j * 3] = rand(1) < 0.5;  g_j += 1; );
  grain_ok = 1;
);
g_j = 0;
loop(1800,
  g_y = VUS[101 + g_j * 3];
  (g_y > 64 && g_y < 322) || g_y > 374 ? (
    col(VUS[102 + g_j * 3] ? 0xFFFFFF : 0x000000, VUS[102 + g_j * 3] ? 0.035 : 0.25);
    gfx_rect(px(VUS[100 + g_j * 3]), py(g_y), max(1, ps(1)), max(1, ps(1)), 1);
  );
  g_j += 1;
);
g_u = 0;
loop(2,
  g_t = g_u ? 330 : 0;  g_hb = g_u ? 44 : 64;  g_h = g_u ? 352 : 322;
  col(C_HEAD, 1);  u_rect(0, g_t, PNL_W, g_hb);
  col(C_ORG, 1);  u_rect(0, g_t + g_hb - 3, PNL_W, 3);                // the orange rule under each top bar
  col(0x0B0C0D, 1);  u_rect(0, g_t + g_hb, PNL_W, 1);
  col(C_ORG, 1);  u_rect(16, g_t + (g_u ? 12 : 13), 4, g_hb - (g_u ? 24 : 28));   // an orange tab beside each unit's name
  col(0xFFFFFF, 0.06);  u_rect(0, g_t, PNL_W, 1);                     // light from above on each unit's top edge
  col(0x000000, 0.55);  u_rect(0, g_t + g_h - 3, PNL_W, 3);  u_rect(PNL_W - 3, g_t, 3, g_h);
  rivet(9, g_t + 9);  rivet(PNL_W - 9, g_t + 9);  rivet(9, g_t + g_h - 9);  rivet(PNL_W - 9, g_t + g_h - 9);
  g_u += 1;
);
gfx_setfont(1);  col(C_LINE, 1);  text_l(px(28), py(26), "VAL60");
gfx_setfont(10);  col(C_ORGL, 1);  text_l(px(30), py(47), "PREAMP STACK");
gfx_setfont(4);  col(C_LINE, 1);  text_l(px(28), py(351), "VAL60");
gfx_setfont(10);  col(C_ORGL, 1);  text_l(px(92), py(352), "COMPRESSOR / OUTPUT");
prs_cur_d > 0 ? ( pr_cur = prs_cur_d; prs_cur_d = 0; );     // PRESET parameter: show a preset loaded by the host
pb_k = preset_bar(300, 15, 34, 250, pr_cur, PRESET_MENU);
pb_k > 0 ? ( prs_dirty = pb_k;  pr_cur = pb_k > 12 ? 1 : pb_k; );
by_key(782, 18, 23, 16);
os_key(920, 21, 22, C_INK, 17);

// ---------- PREAMP STACK ---------- (drawn 10 lower, through oy)
oy = ps(10);
box(16, 74, 1048, 226, "PREAMP STACK", 0, 0);
klab_y = 238;
smark(92, 162, 24, 0, "-10");  smark(92, 162, 24, 1 / 3, "0");  smark(92, 162, 24, 2 / 3, "+10");  smark(92, 162, 24, 1, "+20");
smark(92, 162, 24, 1 / 6, "");  smark(92, 162, 24, 0.5, "");  smark(92, 162, 24, 5 / 6, "");
klab_y = 208;
kn(92, 162, 24, 2, -10, 20, 0, "INPUT GAIN", 2);
gfx_setfont(7);  col(C_INK2, 1);  text_c(px(92), py(224), "dB");
lk_key(50, 240, 84, 26, guard >= 0.5, LK_AMB, "GUARD") ? ( slider(25) = guard >= 0.5 ? 0 : 1;  param_touched(25); );
gord_dec(st_ord);
g_x1 = mod_x(1);  g_x2 = mod_x(2);  g_x3 = mod_x(3);  g_x4 = mod_x(4);  mx_ok = 1;
stage_mod(g_x1, 1, "IRON", 15, 19, 30);
stage_mod(g_x2, 2, "TRANSISTOR", 16, 20, 30);
stage_mod(g_x3, 3, "SOLID STATE", 17, 21, 30);
stage_mod(g_x4, 4, "VALVE", 18, 3, 20);
lk_key(906, 106, 136, 30, v_on >= 0.5, LK_YEL, "PREAMP") ? ( slider(4) = v_on >= 0.5 ? 0 : 1;  param_touched(4); );
sq_key(910, 176, thick >= 0.5, "THICK") ? ( slider(12) = thick >= 0.5 ? 0 : 1;  param_touched(12); );
// the HEATERS pilot lamp: dim while the valves warm, full once settled; dark with no valve in the stack
g_w = wu_disp < 0 ? 0 : 1 - wu_disp;
col(0x000000, 1);  gfx_circle(px(1010), py(187), ps(10), 1, 1);
col(0x3A2410, 1);  gfx_circle(px(1010), py(187), ps(8), 1, 1);
wu_disp >= 0 ? (
  col(0xFFB040, 0.3 + 0.7 * g_w);  gfx_circle(px(1010), py(187), ps(8), 1, 1);
  col(0xFFE6B0, 0.6 * g_w);  gfx_circle(px(1008), py(185), ps(3), 1, 1);
  col(0xFFB040, 0.22 * g_w);  gfx_circle(px(1010), py(187), ps(15), 1, 1);
);
gfx_setfont(7);  col(C_INK, 1);  text_c(px(1010), py(210), "HEATERS");

// ---------- COMPRESSOR ---------- (unit 2: drawn 74 lower, through oy)
oy = ps(74);
// THRESHOLD (large) | ATTACK / RELEASE over RATIO / MAKE-UP | MIX (large), IN under MIX
box(16, 316, 704, 280, "COMPRESSOR", 0, 0);
klab_y = 467;
smark(140, 410, 38, 0, "-20");  smark(140, 410, 38, 0.25, "-10");  smark(140, 410, 38, 0.5, "0");  smark(140, 410, 38, 0.75, "+10");
smark(140, 410, 38, 1, "+20");
kn(140, 410, 38, 5, -20, 20, 0, "THRESHOLD", 1);
klab_y = 443;
smark(314, 398, 26, 0, "1");  smark(314, 398, 26, lt(5, 1, 50), "5");  smark(314, 398, 26, lt(20, 1, 50), "20");  smark(314, 398, 26, 1, "50");
klog = 1;  kn(314, 398, 26, 7, 1, 50, 10, "ATTACK", 4);
smark(450, 398, 26, 0, ".1");  smark(450, 398, 26, lt(500, 100, 4000), ".5");  smark(450, 398, 26, lt(1500, 100, 4000), "1.5");
smark(450, 398, 26, 1, "4");
klog = 1;  kn(450, 398, 26, 8, 100, 4000, 500, "RELEASE", 5);
klab_y = 563;
smark(314, 518, 26, 0, "1.5");  smark(314, 518, 26, lt(3, 1.5, 10), "3");  smark(314, 518, 26, lt(5, 1.5, 10), "5");
smark(314, 518, 26, 1, "10");  smark(314, 518, 26, lt(2, 1.5, 10), "");  smark(314, 518, 26, lt(7, 1.5, 10), "");
klog = 1;  kn(314, 518, 26, 6, 1.5, 10, 3, "RATIO", 3);
smark(450, 518, 26, 0, "0");  smark(450, 518, 26, 0.25, "5");  smark(450, 518, 26, 0.5, "10");  smark(450, 518, 26, 0.75, "15");
smark(450, 518, 26, 1, "20");
kn(450, 518, 26, 13, 0, 20, 0, "MAKE-UP", 2);
klab_y = 467;
smark(610, 410, 38, 0, "DRY");  smark(610, 410, 38, 0.5, "50");  smark(610, 410, 38, 1, "WET");
smark(610, 410, 38, 0.25, "");  smark(610, 410, 38, 0.75, "");
kn(610, 410, 38, 14, 0, 100, 100, "MIX", 7);
gfx_setfont(7);  col(C_INK2, 1);
text_c(px(140), py(483), "dBu");  text_c(px(314), py(458), "ms");  text_c(px(450), py(458), "s");  text_c(px(450), py(578), "dB");
text_c(px(610), py(483), "%");
// GAIN REDUCTION under THRESHOLD: eight round LEDs, blue > green > yellow > orange > red (JG), VU-like ballistics
g_gm = c_in >= 0.5 ? -gr_disp : 0;  gr_disp = 0;
gr_s = g_gm > gr_s ? gr_s + (g_gm - gr_s) * 0.5 : gr_s + (g_gm - gr_s) * 0.12;
g_j = 0;
loop(8,
  g_d = g_j == 0 ? 1 : g_j == 1 ? 2 : g_j == 2 ? 3 : g_j == 3 ? 4 : g_j == 4 ? 6 : g_j == 5 ? 8 : g_j == 6 ? 10 : 15;
  g_c = g_j < 2 ? 0x3A9CFF : g_j < 4 ? 0x3CE05A : g_j == 4 ? 0xFFC81E : g_j == 5 ? 0xFF8A1E : 0xFF3A2A;
  sprintf(#ml, "%d", g_d);
  gfx_setfont(7);  col(C_INK, 1);  text_c(px(72 + g_j * 24), py(508), #ml);
  lamp_k = 1.2;  lamp(72 + g_j * 24, 528, g_c, gr_s >= g_d - 0.01);
  g_j += 1;
);
gfx_setfont(7);  col(C_INK2, 1);  text_c(px(156), py(552), "GAIN REDUCTION  dB");
c_in < 0.5 ? ( col(C_FACE, 0.55);  u_rect(24, 328, 688, 260); );
lk_key(575, 520, 70, 30, c_in >= 0.5, LK_AMB, "IN") ? ( slider(1) = c_in >= 0.5 ? 0 : 1;  param_touched(1); );

// ---------- OUTPUT ----------
box(736, 316, 328, 280, "OUTPUT", 0, 0);
// LEVEL (large) with CLIP and DRIFT under it, the IN / OUT ladders to its right
klab_y = 467;
smark(830, 410, 38, 0, "-18");  smark(830, 410, 38, 0.375, "-9");  smark(830, 410, 38, 0.75, "0");  smark(830, 410, 38, 1, "+6");
smark(830, 410, 38, 0.125, "");  smark(830, 410, 38, 0.25, "");  smark(830, 410, 38, 0.5, "");  smark(830, 410, 38, 0.625, "");  smark(830, 410, 38, 0.875, "");
kn(830, 410, 38, 9, -18, 6, 0, "LEVEL", 2);
gfx_setfont(7);  col(C_INK2, 1);  text_c(px(830), py(483), "dB");
clip_disp ? ( clip_t = time_precise();  clip_disp = 0; );
lamp(792, 532, 0xFF3A2A, time_precise() - clip_t < 0.4);
gfx_setfont(7);  col(C_INK, 1);  text_c(px(792), py(555), "CLIP");
// DRIFT: a two-position key - lit = 33 %, dark = 5 % (a whisper of it)
sq_key(838, 521, drift >= 19, "DRIFT") ? ( slider(10) = drift >= 19 ? 5 : 33;  param_touched(10); );
// IN / OUT: the house LED ladder pair (peak, dBFS), in one dark bezel
g_il = ipk_disp > 0.00001 ? 20 * log10(ipk_disp) : -100;  g_ol = opk_disp > 0.00001 ? 20 * log10(opk_disp) : -100;
ipk_disp = opk_disp = 0;
col(0x2A2B2E, 1);  u_rect(946, 360, 100, 228);
col(0x000000, 0.5);  u_rect(946, 360, 100, 2);  u_rect(946, 360, 2, 228);
vladder(960, 374, 24, 180, g_il, 200);
vladder(1008, 374, 24, 180, g_ol, 202);
gfx_setfont(7);  col(C_INK, 1);  text_c(px(972), py(572), "IN");  text_c(px(1020), py(572), "OUT");

oy = 0;

// ---------- S / M / L / ? (size picker and credits) ----------
g_j = 0;
loop(4,
  g_x = PNL_W - 82 + g_j * 14;  g_on = g_j == 0 ? ui_sz == 1 : g_j == 1 ? ui_sz == 0 : g_j == 2 ? ui_sz == 2 : sz_help;
  col(0x000000, 1);  u_rect(g_x, 23, 13, 18);
  col(g_on ? C_LCDTX : 0x2E2F32, 1);  u_rect(g_x + 1, 24, 11, 16);
  gfx_setfont(7);  col(g_on ? C_LCDBG : 0xC9C1A6, 1);  text_c(px(g_x + 6.5), py(32), g_j == 0 ? "S" : g_j == 1 ? "M" : g_j == 2 ? "L" : "?");
  click && !sz_help && mouse_x >= px(g_x) && mouse_x < px(g_x + 13) && mouse_y >= py(23) && mouse_y < py(41) ? (
    g_j == 0 ? ui_sz = 1 : g_j == 1 ? ui_sz = 0 : g_j == 2 ? ui_sz = 2 : ( sz_help = 1;  sz_new = 1; );
  );
  g_j += 1;
);
sz_help && click && !sz_new ? sz_help = 0;
sz_new = 0;
sz_help ? (
  col(0x000000, 0.62);  gfx_rect(0, 0, gfx_w, gfx_h, 1);
  strcpy(#hl3, "Manual - https://www.gardenfx.uk/manual/");  strcat(#hl3, #ui_man);  strcat(#hl3, ".pdf");
  gfx_setfont(5);  gfx_measurestr(#hl3, g_tw, g_th);
  g_cw = max(g_tw + ps(40), ps(380));  g_ch = ps(130);
  g_cx = (gfx_w - g_cw) * 0.5;  g_cy = (gfx_h - g_ch) * 0.5;
  col(0x000000, 0.5);  ui_rrs(g_cx + ps(3), g_cy + ps(5), g_cw, g_ch, ps(8));
  col(0x1C1D20, 1);    ui_rrs(g_cx, g_cy, g_cw, g_ch, ps(8));
  col(0xE0603A, 1);    gfx_rect(g_cx + ps(20), g_cy + ps(36), g_cw - ps(40), max(1, ps(1)), 1);
  gfx_setfont(6);  col(0xF2F2EE, 1);  gfx_x = g_cx + ps(20);  gfx_y = g_cy + ps(14);  gfx_drawstr("Design by JGWizrad.  © John Garden 2026");
  gfx_setfont(5);  col(0xE8B23A, 1);  gfx_x = g_cx + ps(20);  gfx_y = g_cy + ps(50);  gfx_drawstr("https://www.gardenfx.uk/");
  col(0xD8D6D0, 1);  gfx_x = g_cx + ps(20);  gfx_y = g_cy + ps(72);  gfx_drawstr(#hl3);
  col(0x85837E, 1);  gfx_x = g_cx + ps(20);  gfx_y = g_cy + ps(102);  gfx_drawstr("Click anywhere to close.");
);

!lmb ? drag_idx = 0;
mouse_wheel = 0;
last_lmb = lmb;
